[14.581737, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[5d  \u001b[38;5;252mmethods get 405 with Allow: GET; it's registered at /health. / still serves hello.\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;252m• main_test.go: TestHealth, TestHealthMethodNotAllowed. Nothing has been run here \u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K      \u001b[38;5;252mbecause there's no Go toolchain; the tester needs to run go test ./...\u001b[m               \u001b[38;5;238m│\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;215;48;5;237;1m 👤 \u001b[m \u001b[38;5;217;1m@\u001b[38;5;215mleogr\u001b[38;5;243;22m · you\u001b[m        \u001b[38;5;108m● \u001b[?7h\u001b[7;120H\u001b[m\u001b[8;91H\u001b[1K\r\n \u001b[38;2;123;131;255;1m>_ space-commander\u001b[38;5;243;22m  13:12\u001b[m\u001b[59X\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;110;1m@reviewer\u001b[38;5;252;22m please review commit c361815 on health for GET /health. Reply to \u001b[m         \n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;110;1m@space-commander\u001b[38;5;252;22m with your verdict and findings.\u001b[m\u001b[34X\u001b[12;91H\u001b[1K\r\n \u001b[38;2;123;131;255;1m>_ reviewer\u001b[38;5;243;22m  13:12\u001b[m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;243m↳ space-commander: @reviewer please review commit c361815 on health for GET /he…\u001b[m\n\u001b[6G\u001b[38;5;110;1mspace-commander\u001b[38;5;252;22m Approved c361815 on health. No blocking findings. GET /health returns \u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;252m200 with application/json and {\"status\":\"ok\"} followed by a newline. Other methods \u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;252mreceive 405 with Allow: GET, and / still serves hello.\u001b[m\u001b[18;91H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;252mThe POST test checks the status. Adding an assertion for Allow: GET would cover the \u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;252mfull response contract. git diff --check passed. The Go suite remains unverified here \u001b[m \n\u001b[5G\u001b[38;5;252mbecause this environment has no Go toolchain.\u001b[m\u001b[38X\u001b[22;91H\u001b[1K\r\n \u001b[38;2;123;131;255;1m>_ space-commander\u001b[38;5;243;22m  13:12\u001b[m\n\u001b[5G\u001